  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The structure of the IUPAC compound is</p><p>Secondary prefix+ primary prefix + root word + Primary suffix + Secondary suffix</p><p>It is a cyclic compound, with one <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>OH</mi></math> group on position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> and double bond at position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0131_867e91789a2a.png\" style=\"width: 196px; height: 222px;\"/></p><p>There is no secondary prefix in the above compound. primary prefix is cyclo. Root word is hex, primary suffix is en and secondary suffix is ol.</p><p>Hence, the name is Cyclohex-2-en-1-ol.</p>"
  }
